OL,3,GNEWSAAnger at living with sewage smells
OL,4,Afor a decade
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents on a housing estate have
OL,7,Frenewed calls for something to be done
OL,8,Fas they say they have been living with
OL,9,Fthe smell of sewage for a decade.
OL,11,FThey said the problem in Stourscombe,
OL,12,Fnear Launceston, Cornwall, began when
OL,13,Fsewers from a housing development on
OL,14,Fthe other side of the A388 were
OL,15,Fconnected to the sewers serving the
OL,16,Festate's 400 properties.
OL,18,FResident Les Whaley said he had records
OL,19,Fgoing back to 2016 when the sewage
OL,20,Fsmell first occurred in Snowdrop
OL,21,FCrescent.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
